### Example usage

```tsx
<CheckoutPage
  cartItems={[
    { id: '1', name: 'Wireless Mouse', price: 29.99, quantity: 1 },
    { id: '2', name: 'USB-C Cable', price: 9.99, quantity: 2 },
  ]}
  onBackToCart={() => navigate('/cart')}
  onPay={async (address) => {
    await submitOrder(address);
    navigate('/order-confirmation');
  }}
/>
```

Notes:
- Validation runs on blur and on submit; the Pay button is disabled only while submitting, not while invalid, so users always get field-level error messages instead of a silently disabled button.
- `onPay` can be async (e.g. calling a payment API) — errors are caught and shown inline.
- Swap `shippingCost`/`currencySymbol` or the layout grid to match your shop's actual rules.
